<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49186" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭpūs</span></b> ,
			pŏdis (abl. tripodi, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 1,
		739</span></i>), m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίπους,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a three-footed
			seat</i>, <i>a tripod.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">donarem tripodas, praemia fortium Graiorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 8, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5, 110</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 24</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev. Dial. 2, 1</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>the tripod of
			Pythia</i>, <i>the priestess of Apollo</i>, <i>at Delphi</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 16, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3, 360</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 3,
				789</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 5, 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Med.
				86</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>The oracle at Delphi</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mittitur ad tripodas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 855</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>An oracle</i>, in gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salve, prisca fides tripodum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 1, 509</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 1, 544</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Med.
				785</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
